id: pm-rlm-pdtc
title: Answer evidence coverage for declared question components
description: "Require recursive answers to carry bounded source witnesses for every declared question component, with explicit unsupported and unknown outcomes. Acceptance: replay verifies every witness digest; omitted evidence cannot support an answer; validation performs no hidden model call. Add typed SDK and CLI surfaces, compact TOON/JSON, typed refusals with remedies, documentation and public-tracker no-git validation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:11:52.137Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T15:32:03.027Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-rlm-a1ih
comments[17]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T21:12:22.094Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Overlap checked against the pinned CLI SDK query/aggregate contract, pm-context context-pack/context-handoff and receipt APIs, and pm-rlm aggregate/replay code. Core owns arithmetic, pm-context assembles context bundles and usage receipts, and existing RLM replay certifies execution. None requires evidence coverage per declared question component. Plan: opt-in immutable component declarations, bounded source-witness observations, component-only final answers with supported/unsupported/unknown statuses, deterministic replay and read-only coverage CLI. Builds on PR #13; merge after it. Run targeted local tests/typecheck/lint and use unchanged CI npm/Bun release gates for full evidence."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T21:19:34.179Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Implemented opt-in component contracts and bounded source-witness/answer actions, typed evidence refusals with remedies, deterministic read-only evidence inspection, and a separate read-only source tracker SDK option. First 8 focused regressions passed. Public acceptance used verified public pm-lint revision f2c20efa78139f4071f3dd08d317bea05337fe28: 12 real items, 54941 JSON bytes, 30 read-only source files unchanged; 5 components (3 supported, 1 unsupported, 1 unknown), 3 witnesses of 64/42/89 bytes, 1172-byte JSON report, 4 protocol-fixture steps, zero external inference calls and zero validation model calls. Digest tampering and omitted observation both refused. No provider quality claim."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T21:23:12.641Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Local focused validation: pm test --run --progress executed node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/evidence.test.ts test/core.test.ts test/commands.test.ts with 20/20 passing. Real HTTP command acceptance counted exactly 2 visible provider-fixture requests through run, evidence, replay and completed resume. Behavioral revert proof: node test/evidence-revert.ts passed 3/3; disabling witness admission, trusting persisted witnesses without rehashing, or dropping component completeness each caused the targeted regression to fail by assertion. Authored bytes restored exactly. Typecheck, lint, build, docstring and zero-duplication checks passed; full npm/Bun release checks remain delegated to CI because the shared CPU is saturated."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T21:26:14.433Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "CI first pass exercised 186 tests: 185 passed, with the sole failure in the shallow-clone proof inventory because the new evidence proof adds an eighth script to a fixed seven-script assertion. Updated the inventory to eight. CI reported 100/100/100/100 source coverage, but that failed run is not accepted as a release gate. Also hardened resume so completed evidence checkpoints with no final component-answer step or an omitted unused witness are refused; the updated 13-test evidence suite passes, including legitimate pending-response recovery."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T21:26:53.048Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: Updated the two existing behavioral-proof transform anchors affected by remedy-bearing refusals and CLI remedy formatting. The behavioral mutations and expected failures remain unchanged. A static pass over the committed proof declarations identified these anchors before running the expanded shallow-clone inventory in CI.
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T21:33:35.835Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "CI on 799f1a6 passed 194/194 tests, all eight shallow-clone proof scripts and 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 25 authored source files. Production dependency audit reported zero vulnerabilities. The subsequent packed-install allowlist rejected the two new docs artifacts; extended that exact allowlist without weakening exclusions. Strengthened both packed npm and Bun consumers to execute the new SDK contract and native evidence command in JSON and TOON. Local npm run test:install now passes 2/2; refreshed typecheck/lint/docstring/zero-duplication pass. Full npm/Bun release commands will run again in CI. Documented that source_workspace captures item snapshots while history actions use the ledger tracker."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T21:38:24.511Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Implementation and documentation are complete; PR #15 is ready for review against main and explicitly requires PR #13 to merge first. Local focused tests passed 20/20, refreshed evidence tests 13/13, evidence revert proofs 3/3 and packed npm/Bun consumers 2/2. Typecheck/lint/build/docstrings/zero-duplication/changelog pass. Full CI release evidence is running at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/39679786270; final exact-head run and measured counts will be linked in the PR. Clean CI strict health passes; a pinned 2026.10.18 host can report pm-github artifact version skew with 2026.10.21 artifacts, so no dependency pin or unrelated configuration was changed. Scope limit: provenance and declared coverage are verified, semantic entailment and completeness of natural-language declarations are not. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; releasing the implementation claim while CI finishes."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T12:17:37.390Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "PR #15 round: fetched remote head 895a567 and main a9e3428. GraphQL reports zero review threads and zero reviews, so no outside-diff findings exist. Resolved the squash-stack merge by retaining main final ledger artifacts, Linux crash guards and fifteen storage revert proofs while retaining the evidence docs allowlist and eighth proof script. Verified exact main bytes for nine ledger/tracker artifacts and the original 22-path feature delta; dependency pins match main. Whole-diff self-review covers witness bounds/scope, component completeness, replay/resume tamper refusals, legacy compatibility, CLI remedies and packed npm/Bun surfaces; no additional valid defect established. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun gates and three evidence behavioral proofs follow; no live model calls are needed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T12:18:39.222Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Merge verification: the final item and JSONL history for inherited ledger work are exactly main. The automatic union receipt described a discarded intermediate representation; reconciliation correctly refused to authenticate it after main was selected. Preserved that superseded receipt outside the active tracker instead of rewriting history or forcing a union. No ledger acceptance fields or history bytes from main changed. Source files from the evidence PR are retained, with only main dependency pins integrated. Changelog is regenerated."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T12:19:57.489Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Behavioral revert receipt: linked node test/evidence-revert.ts passed 1/1 command and 3/3 source-only mutations. Removing witness admission, witness rehashing, or complete declared-component coverage independently makes the focused behavioral regression fail with assertion exit 1; source bytes restored after every mutation. Main merge preservation also passed the 22-path feature-delta comparison and nine exact inherited artifact checks. Both project-side and clone-local superseded auto-union receipts are retained outside active stores; strict health will be rechecked. Full release gates run after committing the merge because the shallow-clone proofs verify HEAD."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T12:52:38.814Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Validation update at merged source f6b009a: local npm and Bun full runs each reached 100/100/100/100 coverage but exited at the same inherited 120-second Linux crash-drill behavioral-revert timeout (195/197 cases, one failed proof plus its parent). These are not green release receipts. A clean isolated node test/ledger-storage-revert.ts --review-only retry passed 4/4 proofs, including the timed-out guard, with source bytes restored. Remaining local npm release stages passed: zero production vulnerabilities, 79-file pack allowlist, changelog, publish attestation and 2/2 actual packed npm/Bun consumers. Full exact-source npm/Bun verification is running in manual CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/39781419372 . GitHub confirms the main merge is conflict-free; latest thread read still contains zero review threads or reviews. No thresholds, timeouts or inherited test logic were changed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T12:59:01.188Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Final source gates: manual CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/39781419372 passed both Node 22 and Node 26 at f6b009a8f38e7cd07a7fd52a796b2e9c33ba28d9. Node 26 npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed all 12 release stages, 197/197 suite cases, 124/124 behavioral mutations across eight shallow-clone scripts (8+3+15+51+5+7+25+10), and 2/2 packed npm/Bun consumers, with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todo in the package suites. Coverage remains 100/100/100/100 across 25 authored files; 106 documented declarations, zero duplication, zero production vulnerabilities, 79-file package allowlist, changelog and publish attestation pass. Both local full attempts hit only the inherited host-load timeout; the isolated four-proof retry and complete CI pass independently resolve it. The feature-specific linked proof passed 1/1 command and 3/3 mutations. Strict isolated health passed ten categories with advisory-only findings. No code, dependency threshold, timeout or inherited storage test changed after f6b009a. Remaining writes are this tracker handoff and generated changelog verification. The item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification; no review threads were replied to or resolved and no PR merge or release occurred."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T15:14:58.263Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Review round 2: remote c6da3ba is clean and already contains current main a9e3428. Read all three unresolved CodeRabbit threads and the latest full review; no outside-diff findings. Verify successful-call wording, authenticate recorded evidence remedies at both replay refusal boundaries, and strengthen complete SDK/CLI report assertions. Reuse this feature item and retain append-only history. Add focused real non-git tracker regressions and independent behavioral revert proofs before unchanged-threshold npm/Bun release gates."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T15:26:19.453Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Round 2 implementation: both reviewed remedy gaps are reproduced and fixed. The same-class sweep also rejects injected remedies on parser refusals and ordinary non-evidence tool refusals. Real non-git tracker tests cover completed/interrupted replay, evidence inspection and resume, with zero inference and unchanged item/history bytes on rejection. Complete SDK and native JSON/TOON reports are deep-compared, including packed npm/Bun consumers. README successful-call wording is backed by a typed failed-child regression. The stricter comparison exposed an existing child receipt omission: before the compatibility correction, both new child model/completion-hook tests failed because terminal receipts dropped remedy. Preserve typed remedy receipts, validate their shape, and reconstruct them on replay/reuse. Updated focused suite now passes 20/20, including both child cases. Existing parse/spawn proof anchors were updated without weakening their mutations. Expanded source-only proof runner follows."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T15:28:34.327Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Round 2 first expanded proof attempt: fifteen mutations produced their expected assertion failures before the runner stopped at the replayed-child reconstruction proof, whose baseline check leaked an uncaught typed RlmError rather than producing the required assertion failure. The command exited 1 and did not establish an 18/18 pass. The zero-duplication gate also rejected a five-line repeated positive-verification block. Both findings prompted an assertion-wrapped shared test helper and a fresh verification run. The subsequent correction and verified rerun receipts supersede this unsuccessful attempt; original audit history remains intact."
    edited_at: "2026-10-22T15:32:00.232Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T15:29:26.762Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Correction to the preceding expanded-proof receipt: that success claim was premature. The first expanded run passed its first fifteen mutations, then correctly rejected the replayed-child reconstruction revert with an uncaught typed RlmError instead of the required assertion failure. The proof runner therefore exited 1; no 18/18 success is accepted from that attempt. The duplication gate also found a five-line repeated positive-verification block. Consolidate that block into an assertion-wrapped helper, then rerun the proof runner and unchanged zero-duplication gate. Earlier 20/20 baseline and before-fix child failures remain valid; history is preserved append-only."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T15:32:03.025Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Verified round 2 proof rerun: pm test pm-rlm-pdtc --run --only-index 2 --progress exits 0 with 1/1 linked command, all 18/18 mutations producing assertion exit 1, and zero assertion, timeout or trust failures in the runner. All authored bytes are restored. The unsuccessful first expanded attempt is corrected through a supported comment edit plus an append-only correction note; no JSONL record was changed. This receipt supersedes that attempt. The proof count is the original three plus nine review proofs and six child-receipt compatibility proofs. Final full release verification remains pending."
